  "articleBody": "Choosing the right shower seat can really up your bathroom's game, whether it's for comfort, safety, or accessibility. First things first, you've got to consider how it'll attach to your wall. Is your shower wall sturdy enough to support it, especially if it's tiled, acrylic, or fiberglass? You'll want to make sure there’s proper blocking or studs behind the wall to anchor the seat securely. Another biggie is the weight it needs to support. Manufacturers usually have clear weight ratings, so check that to ensure it's up to snuff for everyone who'll be using it. Don't forget about the height; an ADA-style seat usually sits between 17\"-19\" from the floor, but your local codes and personal comfort might sway that a bit. Lastly, think about the materials – you want something corrosion-resistant that can stand up to a wet environment. Getting this right from the start can save you a lot of hassle later. If you're unsure about your wall's readiness or need to meet specific accessibility requirements, it's always smart to get a professional like HH Remodeling LLC involved. We can help you navigate these choices and ensure a safe, secure installation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
